      "answer": "$p=-30$, $q=72$.",
      "official_mark_scheme_text": "Use $f(3)=0$ - M1: $2\\times3^3-4\\times3^2+3p+q=0$. Obtain $3p+q=-18$ - A1; OE; powers should be evaluated but need not be simplified. Use $f'(3)=0$ - M1: $54-24+p=0$. Obtain $p=-30$ - A1; OE. Obtain $p=-30,q=72$ - A1; correct only.\n\nAlternative method 1: attempt division of $f(x)$ by $(x-3)^2$ as far as $(2x+Q)$, $Q\\ne0$ - M1. Obtain quotient $(2x+8)$ - A1. Equate the linear remainder to zero and compare coefficients, or expand $(2x+8)(x-3)^2$ and compare coefficients; method to obtain an equation in $p$ or $q$ - M1. Obtain one of $p=-30,q=72$ - A1. Obtain both - A1; correct answers only.\n\nAlternative method 2: use $f(3)=0$ - M1: $54-36+3p+q=0$. Obtain $3p+q=-18$ - A1; OE; powers evaluated. Divide by $(x-3)^2$ as far as $(2x+Q)$ and form an equation in $p$ only, $q$ only, or in $p,q$ - M1. Guidance: in a hybrid method, work towards a second equation from remainder coefficients or use $f(-4)=0$ or equivalent for their $(2x+8)$. Obtain a correct equation - A1. Obtain $p=-30,q=72$ - A1; correct only.\n\nAlternative method 3: $f'(x)=6x^2-8x+p$ - B1. Write $(x-3)(6x+10)$ - M1, using factor $x-3$. Obtain $p=-30$ - A1. Write $f(x)=(x-3)^2(2x+Q)=2x^3-4x^2-30x+q$ - M1, using factor $(x-3)^2$. Hence $Q=8,q=72$ - A1.\n\nAlternative method 4: expand $f(x)=(x-3)^2(Ax+B)$ and compare at least one coefficient other than $x^3$ - M1; $A=2$ may be found by inspection. Obtain $q=9B$ and $p=9A-6B$, or $B=8$ - A1. Use their $A,B$ to solve for $p$ or $q$ - M1 ($A=2,B=8$). Obtain one of $p=-30,q=72$ - A1. Obtain both - A1; correct answer only.\n\nPrinted total: 5.",
